================================================================================
1. RC9 - the defect, reproduced and then fixed
================================================================================

`agent context/TRUNCATED_FILES_REPORT.md` RC9 quotes this from a real /compact:

    - you asked: can you make me a 3d asteroid game...
    - you asked: That reply was empty. Answer the question, or call one tool.
    - you asked: That reply was empty. Answer the question, or call one tool.
    - you asked: okay read from the plan and do the next task please

Two of those four lines are the harness talking to itself. Reproduced against
the same input, old rule vs shipped rule:

$ python -c "<old _digest rule> vs shamsu.agents.simple_chat._digest"

BEFORE (old rule):
- you asked: can you make me a 3d asteroid game
- you asked: That reply was empty. Answer the question, or call one tool.
- you asked: That reply was empty. Answer the question, or call one tool.
- you asked: okay read from the plan and do the next task please

AFTER  (shipped):
- you asked: can you make me a 3d asteroid game
- you asked: okay read from the plan and do the next task please

Root cause was NOT a missing tag. `origin=ORIGIN_LOOP` was already passed at
10 of the 11 loop injection sites and already written to messages.jsonl. It
was dropped twice on the way to the consumer:

  ChatMessage (chat_state.py)   had no `origin` field  -> in-memory readers blind
  _hydrate_records              never read `origin`     -> lost again on resume
  _digest (simple_chat.py)      `if role == "user"`     -> RC9's quoted line

Plus simple_chat.py:2772, the contract nudge, was the one injection site with
no tag at all.

================================================================================
2. _history_pressure - the claim I made, and the measurement that refuted it
================================================================================

Claimed in the review: pressure is measured against every hydrated message
rather than the tail that is sent, so the aggressive elision branch fires from
round one on a resumed thread. The measurement says the mis-measurement is
REAL but INERT - the only consumer compares it to ELIDE_PRESSURE_FRACTION
(0.6), and both measures cross 0.6 at the same archive size.

 archive tokens  old ratio  new ratio  old fires  new fires  differ
          2,263       0.12       0.09      False      False
          4,735       0.24       0.21      False      False
          8,855       0.46       0.43      False      False
         17,115       0.88       0.85       True       True
         33,635       1.74       0.94       True       True
         66,675       3.44       0.94       True       True
        132,875       6.86       0.94       True       True
        265,355      13.69       0.94       True       True

Never disagrees. Kept as a correctness fix (the number now means what it says
and is bounded by what is sent, from the same source of truth
_compact_if_needed uses), NOT as a performance fix. Pinned by
test_the_honest_ratio_never_changes_which_branch_is_taken so nobody expects a
delta from it and nobody later reverts it as "equivalent" - it is equivalent
for exactly one comparison.

