5. Concurrency warning - read before trusting any measurement from tonight
================================================================================

This checkout is being edited by another agent in parallel. Observed during
this task:
  - HEAD moved f0158c2 -> 4e173fe mid-session
  - uncommitted work in shamsu/cli/tui.py, repl.py, live_console.py,
    tests/test_tui.py, PROGRESS_LOG.md, logs/test-runs/2026-08-22-framed-tui.log
  - shamsu/agents/chat_state.py gained new _HARNESS_STATUS_PREFIXES and
    _HARNESS_STATUS_PATTERNS entries WHILE this task was editing the same file
    (no conflict; both sets of changes coexist)

This matters for the eval: the default eval driver is
`shamsu.cli.noninteractive.run_prompt`, which imports repl.py - so the other
agent's in-flight work is ON the eval's code path. scripts/overnight-eval.ps1
records `git status` and HEAD at both start and end of the run so the morning
can tell whether the tree moved underneath it. If those two differ, the run is
not a baseline.

A clean A/B was considered and rejected: `git stash` on a tree another agent is
writing to risks losing their work, and a git worktree cannot isolate the code
because shamsu is installed EDITABLE into .venv - PYTHONPATH does not override
the editable finder (verified: a worktree checkout still imported
F:\Work\PROJECTS\shamsu\Shamsu\shamsu\__init__.py).

