================================================================================
7. THE TREE DRIFTED DURING THE RUN - measured, not hypothesised
================================================================================

The provenance capture caught real drift on its first outing. Files modified
at START vs END of one 14.6-minute run:

  new during the run:  shamsu/control/runner.py
                       shamsu/runtime/turn_stream.py
                       shamsu/webui/api.py, cli.py, local.py
                       shamsu/webui/static/app.css, app.js
                       tests/test_webui.py
                       tests/test_web_access.py            (untracked)
                       logs/test-runs/2026-08-23-web-portal-phases.log

Ten files in fifteen minutes: the other agent started a web-portal task while
the eval was running.

Does it reach the eval? YES for at least one path. `run_prompt` lazily imports
`shamsu.cli.repl` (noninteractive.py:205-206), repl.py has uncommitted changes,
and repl.py pulls TurnStream - so shamsu/runtime/turn_stream.py, modified
mid-run, is reachable from the code under test. The webui files are not.

Consequence: cases 1-8 and cases 9-16 of that run did not necessarily execute
the same code. That is fine for a smoke test and fatal for a baseline. A
3.6-hour unattended run has ~14x more opportunity for the same thing.
